{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf7DPhtHXabYuKmBMs9cE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll author the recipe. The metering boundary and the unresolved ownership both get recorded explicitly rather than invented."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":845,"cache_read_input_tokens":29246,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":845},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f44e1a05-29ac-466d-82d1-9c0b45beda30","uuid":"c4cdf809-7c27-41f0-bd1c-4fd75f6aaea0","timestamp":"2026-09-16T13:41:26.701Z","request_id":"req_011Cf7DPhPmrw53EH32XXpYF"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf7DPhtHXabYuKmBMs9cE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QnHAZbF4XPwvvHf99Q8HuE","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat c_8veas4/.taskspec/authoring-scratch/rate-limiting/rate-limiting-recipe.yaml","content":"schema_version: 1\n\nintent:\n  id: INT-RATELIMIT\n  title: Organization-scoped request rate limiting steel thread\n  summary: >-\n    Deliver a versioned rate-limit policy that validates its own limits and\n    windows, resolves to exactly one effective policy per organization, denies\n    request 101 after 100 allowed requests in the same window, and returns a\n    stable denial reason with matching decision telemetry. Provider-owned usage\n    metering stays outside this initiative.\n  claim: proposed\n  source:\n    uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    captured_at: '2026-09-16T13:40:45Z'\n    sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n  success:\n    - A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and invalid windows.\n    - Policy resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n    - Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n    - A denial returns a stable reason code and emits matching decision telemetry.\n  out_of_scope:\n    - Provider-owned usage metering, which this initiative neither implements nor wraps.\n    - Selection of production storage for policies or counters.\n    - Selection of deployment infrastructure.\n\nsystem_map:\n  claim: proposed\n  components:\n    - Versioned rate-limit policy schema and its validator.\n    - Organization policy resolver producing one effective policy.\n    - Window-scoped request admission decision point.\n    - Denial reason contract and decision telemetry emitter.\n  external_dependencies:\n    - Provider-owned usage metering, which remains the provider's responsibility\n      and is read-only context to this initiative at most.\n  unknowns:\n    - The responsible owner for each seam is not named in the source blueprint.\n    - Window accounting semantics are unstated; fixed versus sliding window is undecided.\n    - The policy and counter storage substrate is deliberately unselected by the blueprint.\n    - The destination sink for decision telemetry is unstated.\n    - Precedence rules when several policies match one organization are unstated.\n\nevidence:\n  - id: EV-BLUEPRINT\n    claim: proposed\n    source:\n      uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      captured_at: '2026-09-16T13:40:45Z'\n      sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n    confidence: 0.6\n    summary: >-\n      Declares the four-step steel thread order and the two scope boundaries.\n      The file states it is fixture input and not documentation of shipped\n      behavior, so it evidences intent, not current system state.\n  - id: EV-EMPTY-BACKLOG\n    claim: current\n    source:\n      uri: tasks\n      captured_at: '2026-09-16T13:40:45Z'\n      sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n    confidence: 0.5\n    summary: >-\n      The repository backlog holds no prior rate-limiting task, so no existing\n      sealed contract constrains this topology. Digest carried from the only\n      readable source file in the fixture; treat as reported, not verified.\n\ndecisions:\n  - id: DEC-METERING-BOUNDARY\n    status: accepted\n    owner: source blueprint tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    rationale: >-\n      Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope. Decision telemetry emitted\n      by this initiative describes admission decisions only and is not a usage\n      meter, not a billing record, and not a substitute for provider metering.\n  - id: DEC-NO-INFRA-SELECTION\n    status: accepted\n    owner: source blueprint tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    rationale: >-\n      Production storage and deployment infrastructure are not selected here, so\n      every leaf must stay behind an in-process interface with a test substrate.\n  - id: DEC-WINDOW-SEMANTICS\n    status: proposed\n    owner: UNASSIGNED pending named product owner\n    rationale: >-\n      Fixed versus sliding window changes the meaning of \"the same window\" in\n      steel thread step 3. Unresolved; recorded rather than chosen.\n\nseams:\n  - id: SEAM-POLICY\n    name: Policy definition and validation\n    description: >-\n      Owns the versioned rate-limit policy schema and the validation that\n      rejects invalid limits and invalid windows before any policy is stored.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Define the versioned policy shape and reject invalid limits and windows.\n      Does not resolve policies and does not count requests.\n    consumes:\n      - candidate policy documents\n    produces:\n      - versioned policy schema\n      - policy validation verdict\n    owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n    independent_proof: >-\n      Validation tests accept a valid policy and reject invalid limits and\n      invalid windows, with no resolver or counter present.\n    decision_ids:\n      - DEC-NO-INFRA-SELECTION\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Validate limits inline at the admission decision point.\n        reason: >-\n          Defers detection of invalid policy to request time and couples the\n          schema to enforcement, removing independent proof of step 1.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-POLICY\n      name: Policy schema lane\n      owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-POLICY-VALID\n          observable_state: >-\n            A versioned policy document is accepted only when its limit and\n            window are valid.\n          proof: Schema validation test suite passes over valid and invalid fixtures.\n          requires: []\n          produces:\n            - versioned policy schema\n            - policy validation verdict\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260916-policy-schema\n              title: Versioned policy schema with limit and window validation\n              goal: >-\n                Introduce a versioned rate-limit policy schema whose validator\n                rejects invalid limits and invalid windows.\n              done_condition: >-\n                A valid policy validates, a non-positive or non-integer limit is\n                rejected, and a non-positive or unparsable window is rejected,\n                each with a distinct validation error, and the schema carries an\n                explicit version field.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on: []\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/policy_schema.py\n                - tests/ratelimit/test_policy_schema.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: A policy document with limit 100 and a well-formed window.\n                  when: The policy validator runs.\n                  then: Validation succeeds and reports the schema version.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: A policy document with limit 0 or an unparsable window.\n                  when: The policy validator runs.\n                  then: >-\n                    Validation fails with a distinct error naming the offending\n                    field, and no policy is produced.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: A valid versioned policy is accepted.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_policy_schema.py -k valid_policy -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Invalid limits and windows are rejected with distinct errors.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_policy_schema.py -k invalid -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: The whole policy schema suite passes.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_policy_schema.py -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Reading or writing provider usage metering data.\n                  reason: Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope.\n                  instead: Validate only the policy document supplied to this leaf.\n                - action: Selecting a database or migration tool for policy storage.\n                  reason: Production storage is not selected by this initiative.\n                  instead: Keep the schema storage-agnostic and validate in memory.\n                - action: Choosing fixed or sliding window semantics to unblock validation.\n                  reason: DEC-WINDOW-SEMANTICS is unresolved and is not this leaf's to decide.\n                  instead: Validate window well-formedness only and leave accounting undecided.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - Any provider usage metering client, schema, or record.\n                - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n              rollback: Remove the created schema and test files; no other module imports them.\n              observability: Validation errors name the offending field and the schema version.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - design\n                - build\n                - test\n\n  - id: SEAM-RESOLUTION\n    name: Effective policy resolution\n    description: >-\n      Owns resolution from an organization identifier to exactly one effective\n      policy, including the ambiguity and absence outcomes.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Produce exactly one effective policy for an organization, or a definite\n      no-policy outcome. Does not define the schema and does not count requests.\n    consumes:\n      - versioned policy schema\n      - organization identifier\n    produces:\n      - effective policy for an organization\n    owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n    independent_proof: >-\n      Resolution tests show exactly one effective policy for an organization and\n      a deterministic outcome when zero or several candidates match, with no\n      request counting involved.\n    decision_ids:\n      - DEC-NO-INFRA-SELECTION\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Let the admission point pick among matching policies at request time.\n        reason: >-\n          Makes \"exactly one effective policy\" unobservable on its own and hides\n          ambiguity inside enforcement.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-RESOLUTION\n      name: Resolution lane\n      owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-RESOLVE-ONE\n          observable_state: >-\n            Resolving an organization yields exactly one effective policy or a\n            definite no-policy outcome.\n          proof: Resolver test suite passes over zero, one, and several candidates.\n          requires:\n            - versioned policy schema\n          produces:\n            - effective policy for an organization\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260916-policy-resolver\n              title: Resolve exactly one effective policy per organization\n              goal: >-\n                Given validated policies, resolve an organization to exactly one\n                effective policy with a deterministic outcome in every case.\n              done_condition: >-\n                Resolution returns one effective policy when candidates exist,\n                returns an explicit no-policy outcome when none match, and is\n                deterministic and non-silent when several candidates match.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on:\n                - T-20260916-policy-schema\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/resolver.py\n                - tests/ratelimit/test_resolver.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: One validated policy matches an organization.\n                  when: Resolution runs for that organization.\n                  then: Exactly that policy is returned as the effective policy.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: Zero or several validated policies match an organization.\n                  when: Resolution runs for that organization.\n                  then: >-\n                    A deterministic, explicit outcome is returned; the resolver\n                    never silently returns several policies.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: A single matching policy resolves to itself.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_resolver.py -k single_match -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Zero and multiple candidate cases are deterministic and explicit.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_resolver.py -k \"no_match or ambiguous\" -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: The whole resolver suite passes.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_resolver.py -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Deriving the effective policy from provider usage metering.\n                  reason: Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope.\n                  instead: Resolve only from validated policy documents and the organization id.\n                - action: Introducing a persistence layer or cache to hold policies.\n                  reason: Production storage is not selected by this initiative.\n                  instead: Resolve over an in-memory collection behind a narrow interface.\n                - action: Inventing a precedence rule when several policies match.\n                  reason: Precedence is an unresolved product decision recorded in system_map.unknowns.\n                  instead: Surface ambiguity explicitly and leave the precedence rule to the owner.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - Any provider usage metering client, schema, or record.\n                - src/ratelimit/policy_schema.py\n              rollback: Remove the created resolver and test files.\n              observability: The resolution outcome names the organization and the chosen policy version.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - build\n                - test\n\n  - id: SEAM-ENFORCEMENT\n    name: Window-scoped admission decision\n    description: >-\n      Owns the counting of requests inside a window against the effective policy\n      and the allow or deny verdict for each request.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Decide allow or deny for a request against the effective policy within the\n      window. Does not define policies and does not emit telemetry.\n    consumes:\n      - effective policy for an organization\n      - request arrival\n    produces:\n      - admission decision\n    owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n    independent_proof: >-\n      Given a fixed effective policy of 100 per window, the first 100 requests\n      are allowed and request 101 in the same window is denied, with no telemetry\n      sink attached.\n    decision_ids:\n      - DEC-NO-INFRA-SELECTION\n      - DEC-WINDOW-SEMANTICS\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Derive the request count from provider usage metering counters.\n        reason: >-\n          Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope, and borrowing its\n          counters would place the denial decision on the far side of the boundary.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-ENFORCEMENT\n      name: Enforcement lane\n      owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-DENY-101\n          observable_state: >-\n            After 100 allowed requests in one window, request 101 is denied.\n          proof: Admission test suite drives 101 requests against a 100-per-window policy.\n          requires:\n            - effective policy for an organization\n          produces:\n            - admission decision\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260916-admission-decision\n              title: Deny request 101 after 100 allowed in the same window\n              goal: >-\n                Count requests within a window against the effective policy and\n                deny once the limit is exceeded.\n              done_condition: >-\n                With an effective policy of 100 per window, requests 1 through\n                100 are allowed and request 101 in the same window is denied;\n                the counter is scoped per organization and per window.\n              effort: M\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on:\n                - T-20260916-policy-resolver\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/admission.py\n                - tests/ratelimit/test_admission.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: An effective policy of 100 requests per window for an organization.\n                  when: Requests 1 through 100 arrive in the same window.\n                  then: Every one of those requests is allowed.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: 100 requests already allowed in the current window.\n                  when: Request 101 arrives in the same window.\n                  then: The request is denied and the counter is not incremented past the limit.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: The first 100 requests in a window are allowed.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_admission.py -k allows_first_100 -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Request 101 in the same window is denied.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_admission.py -k denies_101 -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: The whole admission suite passes.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_admission.py -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Reading provider usage metering counters to decide admission.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope; the denial\n                    decision must not depend on it.\n                  instead: Count against this initiative's own window counter behind its interface.\n                - action: Selecting Redis or another counter store.\n                  reason: Production storage is not selected by this initiative.\n                  instead: Keep the counter behind an interface with an in-memory test substrate.\n                - action: Emitting telemetry from inside the decision function.\n                  reason: Telemetry is SEAM-TELEMETRY's responsibility and would blur the seam.\n                  instead: Return a structured decision and let the telemetry seam observe it.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - Any provider usage metering client, schema, or record.\n                - src/ratelimit/policy_schema.py\n                - src/ratelimit/resolver.py\n              rollback: Remove the created admission and test files.\n              observability: The decision carries organization, window, count, and limit.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - build\n                - test\n\n  - id: SEAM-TELEMETRY\n    name: Denial reason and decision telemetry\n    description: >-\n      Owns the stable denial reason contract and the emission of decision\n      telemetry that matches the decision actually made.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Expose a stable denial reason and emit decision telemetry that matches it.\n      This telemetry describes admission decisions and is explicitly not a usage\n      meter and not a replacement for provider-owned metering.\n    consumes:\n      - admission decision\n    produces:\n      - stable denial reason\n      - decision telemetry event\n    owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n    independent_proof: >-\n      A denial yields a reason code that is stable across runs, and the emitted\n      telemetry event matches that same decision field for field.\n    decision_ids:\n      - DEC-METERING-BOUNDARY\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Emit the decision onto the provider usage metering stream.\n        reason: >-\n          That crosses the stated boundary and would make this initiative a\n          partial usage meter, which the blueprint places out of scope.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-TELEMETRY\n      name: Telemetry lane\n      owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-REASON-TELEMETRY\n          observable_state: >-\n            A denial returns a stable reason and emits one matching decision\n            telemetry event.\n          proof: Telemetry test suite asserts reason stability and event-to-decision agreement.\n          requires:\n            - admission decision\n          produces:\n            - stable denial reason\n            - decision telemetry event\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260916-denial-telemetry\n              title: Stable denial reason with matching decision telemetry\n              goal: >-\n                Give every denial a stable reason code and emit one decision\n                telemetry event that agrees with the decision.\n              done_condition: >-\n                A denial returns the same reason code on repeated runs, exactly\n                one telemetry event is emitted per decision, the event fields\n                agree with the decision, and no event is written to any provider\n                usage metering sink.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on:\n                - T-20260916-admission-decision\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/telemetry.py\n                - tests/ratelimit/test_telemetry.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: A request denied for exceeding the window limit.\n                  when: The denial is returned twice for the same condition.\n                  then: The same stable reason code is returned both times.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: An admission decision is made.\n                  when: Telemetry is emitted for that decision.\n                  then: >-\n                    Exactly one event is emitted to the decision telemetry sink\n                    and its fields match the decision.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: The denial reason code is stable across repeated denials.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_telemetry.py -k stable_reason -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: One emitted event per decision, matching its fields.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_telemetry.py -k matching_event -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: The whole telemetry suite passes.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_telemetry.py -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Writing decision events to a provider usage metering sink.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope; decision\n                    telemetry must not be presented or routed as usage data.\n                  instead: Emit to this initiative's own decision telemetry interface.\n                - action: Adding billable-usage fields such as metered units or cost.\n                  reason: Those fields belong to provider-owned metering, not to this seam.\n                  instead: Carry only decision fields: organization, policy version, reason, outcome.\n                - action: Selecting a hosted observability vendor or exporter.\n                  reason: Deployment infrastructure is not selected by this initiative.\n                  instead: Emit behind a sink interface with a recording test double.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - Any provider usage metering client, schema, sink, or record.\n                - src/ratelimit/admission.py\n              rollback: Remove the created telemetry and test files.\n              observability: >-\n                The decision telemetry event is the observability surface; it is\n                scoped to admission decisions only.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - build\n                - test\n                - maintain\n\nsteel_thread:\n  - SEAM-POLICY\n  - SEAM-RESOLUTION\n  - SEAM-ENFORCEMENT\n  - SEAM-TELEMETRY\n\nobjections:\n  - id: OBJ-NO-OWNER\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      No seam, swimlane, or decision owner is named anywhere in the source\n      blueprint. Every owner field carries an explicit unassigned marker rather\n      than an invented identity. Named owners are required before review.\n  - id: OBJ-WINDOW-SEMANTICS\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      Fixed versus sliding window is undecided (DEC-WINDOW-SEMANTICS), and it\n      changes what \"the same window\" means in steel thread step 3, so the\n      enforcement done-condition is not yet fully determined.\n  - id: OBJ-PRECEDENCE\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      The blueprint requires exactly one effective policy but states no\n      precedence rule for several matching policies. The resolver leaf surfaces\n      ambiguity explicitly instead of inventing precedence.\n  - id: OBJ-FIXTURE-EVIDENCE\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      The only evidence source declares itself fixture input and not\n      documentation of shipped behavior, so the system map is proposed rather\n      than verified against a running system.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":845,"cache_read_input_tokens":29246,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":845},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f44e1a05-29ac-466d-82d1-9c0b45beda30","uuid":"d0a19362-61e4-429c-a36d-83537173be65","timestamp":"2026-09-16T13:42:54.828Z","request_id":"req_011Cf7DPhPmrw53EH32XXpYF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QnHAZbF4XPwvvHf99Q8HuE":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat c_8veas4/.taskspec/authoring-scratch/rate-limiting/rate-limiting-recipe.yaml","content":"schema_version: 1\n\nintent:\n  id: INT-RATELIMIT\n  title: Organization-scoped request rate limiting steel thread\n  summary: >-\n    Deliver a versioned rate-limit policy that validates its own limits and\n    windows, resolves to exactly one effective policy per organization, denies\n    request 101 after 100 allowed requests in the same window, and returns a\n    stable denial reason with matching decision telemetry. Provider-owned usage\n    metering stays outside this initiative.\n  claim: proposed\n  source:\n    uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    captured_at: '2026-09-16T13:40:45Z'\n    sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n  success:\n    - A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and invalid windows.\n    - Policy resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n    - Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n    - A denial returns a stable reason code and emits matching decision telemetry.\n  out_of_scope:\n    - Provider-owned usage metering, which this initiative neither implements nor wraps.\n    - Selection of production storage for policies or counters.\n    - Selection of deployment infrastructure.\n\nsystem_map:\n  claim: proposed\n  components:\n    - Versioned rate-limit policy schema and its validator.\n    - Organization policy resolver producing one effective policy.\n    - Window-scoped request admission decision point.\n    - Denial reason contract and decision telemetry emitter.\n  external_dependencies:\n    - Provider-owned usage metering, which remains the provider's responsibility\n      and is read-only context to this initiative at most.\n  unknowns:\n    - The responsible owner for each seam is not named in the source blueprint.\n    - Window accounting semantics are unstated; fixed versus sliding window is undecided.\n    - The policy and counter storage substrate is deliberately unselected by the blueprint.\n    - The destination sink for decision telemetry is unstated.\n    - Precedence rules when several policies match one organization are unstated.\n\nevidence:\n  - id: EV-BLUEPRINT\n    claim: proposed\n    source:\n      uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      captured_at: '2026-09-16T13:40:45Z'\n      sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n    confidence: 0.6\n    summary: >-\n      Declares the four-step steel thread order and the two scope boundaries.\n      The file states it is fixture input and not documentation of shipped\n      behavior, so it evidences intent, not current system state.\n  - id: EV-EMPTY-BACKLOG\n    claim: current\n    source:\n      uri: tasks\n      captured_at: '2026-09-16T13:40:45Z'\n      sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n    confidence: 0.5\n    summary: >-\n      The repository backlog holds no prior rate-limiting task, so no existing\n      sealed contract constrains this topology. Digest carried from the only\n      readable source file in the fixture; treat as reported, not verified.\n\ndecisions:\n  - id: DEC-METERING-BOUNDARY\n    status: accepted\n    owner: source blueprint tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    rationale: >-\n      Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope. Decision telemetry emitted\n      by this initiative describes admission decisions only and is not a usage\n      meter, not a billing record, and not a substitute for provider metering.\n  - id: DEC-NO-INFRA-SELECTION\n    status: accepted\n    owner: source blueprint tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    rationale: >-\n      Production storage and deployment infrastructure are not selected here, so\n      every leaf must stay behind an in-process interface with a test substrate.\n  - id: DEC-WINDOW-SEMANTICS\n    status: proposed\n    owner: UNASSIGNED pending named product owner\n    rationale: >-\n      Fixed versus sliding window changes the meaning of \"the same window\" in\n      steel thread step 3. Unresolved; recorded rather than chosen.\n\nseams:\n  - id: SEAM-POLICY\n    name: Policy definition and validation\n    description: >-\n      Owns the versioned rate-limit policy schema and the validation that\n      rejects invalid limits and invalid windows before any policy is stored.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Define the versioned policy shape and reject invalid limits and windows.\n      Does not resolve policies and does not count requests.\n    consumes:\n      - candidate policy documents\n    produces:\n      - versioned policy schema\n      - policy validation verdict\n    owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n    independent_proof: >-\n      Validation tests accept a valid policy and reject invalid limits and\n      invalid windows, with no resolver or counter present.\n    decision_ids:\n      - DEC-NO-INFRA-SELECTION\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Validate limits inline at the admission decision point.\n        reason: >-\n          Defers detection of invalid policy to request time and couples the\n          schema to enforcement, removing independent proof of step 1.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-POLICY\n      name: Policy schema lane\n      owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-POLICY-VALID\n          observable_state: >-\n            A versioned policy document is accepted only when its limit and\n            window are valid.\n          proof: Schema validation test suite passes over valid and invalid fixtures.\n          requires: []\n          produces:\n            - versioned policy schema\n            - policy validation verdict\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260916-policy-schema\n              title: Versioned policy schema with limit and window validation\n              goal: >-\n                Introduce a versioned rate-limit policy schema whose validator\n                rejects invalid limits and invalid windows.\n              done_condition: >-\n                A valid policy validates, a non-positive or non-integer limit is\n                rejected, and a non-positive or unparsable window is rejected,\n                each with a distinct validation error, and the schema carries an\n                explicit version field.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on: []\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/policy_schema.py\n                - tests/ratelimit/test_policy_schema.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: A policy document with limit 100 and a well-formed window.\n                  when: The policy validator runs.\n                  then: Validation succeeds and reports the schema version.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: A policy document with limit 0 or an unparsable window.\n                  when: The policy validator runs.\n                  then: >-\n                    Validation fails with a distinct error naming the offending\n                    field, and no policy is produced.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: A valid versioned policy is accepted.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_policy_schema.py -k valid_policy -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Invalid limits and windows are rejected with distinct errors.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_policy_schema.py -k invalid -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: The whole policy schema suite passes.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_policy_schema.py -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Reading or writing provider usage metering data.\n                  reason: Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope.\n                  instead: Validate only the policy document supplied to this leaf.\n                - action: Selecting a database or migration tool for policy storage.\n                  reason: Production storage is not selected by this initiative.\n                  instead: Keep the schema storage-agnostic and validate in memory.\n                - action: Choosing fixed or sliding window semantics to unblock validation.\n                  reason: DEC-WINDOW-SEMANTICS is unresolved and is not this leaf's to decide.\n                  instead: Validate window well-formedness only and leave accounting undecided.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - Any provider usage metering client, schema, or record.\n                - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n              rollback: Remove the created schema and test files; no other module imports them.\n              observability: Validation errors name the offending field and the schema version.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - design\n                - build\n                - test\n\n  - id: SEAM-RESOLUTION\n    name: Effective policy resolution\n    description: >-\n      Owns resolution from an organization identifier to exactly one effective\n      policy, including the ambiguity and absence outcomes.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Produce exactly one effective policy for an organization, or a definite\n      no-policy outcome. Does not define the schema and does not count requests.\n    consumes:\n      - versioned policy schema\n      - organization identifier\n    produces:\n      - effective policy for an organization\n    owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n    independent_proof: >-\n      Resolution tests show exactly one effective policy for an organization and\n      a deterministic outcome when zero or several candidates match, with no\n      request counting involved.\n    decision_ids:\n      - DEC-NO-INFRA-SELECTION\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Let the admission point pick among matching policies at request time.\n        reason: >-\n          Makes \"exactly one effective policy\" unobservable on its own and hides\n          ambiguity inside enforcement.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-RESOLUTION\n      name: Resolution lane\n      owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-RESOLVE-ONE\n          observable_state: >-\n            Resolving an organization yields exactly one effective policy or a\n            definite no-policy outcome.\n          proof: Resolver test suite passes over zero, one, and several candidates.\n          requires:\n            - versioned policy schema\n          produces:\n            - effective policy for an organization\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260916-policy-resolver\n              title: Resolve exactly one effective policy per organization\n              goal: >-\n                Given validated policies, resolve an organization to exactly one\n                effective policy with a deterministic outcome in every case.\n              done_condition: >-\n                Resolution returns one effective policy when candidates exist,\n                returns an explicit no-policy outcome when none match, and is\n                deterministic and non-silent when several candidates match.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on:\n                - T-20260916-policy-schema\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/resolver.py\n                - tests/ratelimit/test_resolver.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: One validated policy matches an organization.\n                  when: Resolution runs for that organization.\n                  then: Exactly that policy is returned as the effective policy.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: Zero or several validated policies match an organization.\n                  when: Resolution runs for that organization.\n                  then: >-\n                    A deterministic, explicit outcome is returned; the resolver\n                    never silently returns several policies.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: A single matching policy resolves to itself.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_resolver.py -k single_match -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Zero and multiple candidate cases are deterministic and explicit.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_resolver.py -k \"no_match or ambiguous\" -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: The whole resolver suite passes.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_resolver.py -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Deriving the effective policy from provider usage metering.\n                  reason: Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope.\n                  instead: Resolve only from validated policy documents and the organization id.\n                - action: Introducing a persistence layer or cache to hold policies.\n                  reason: Production storage is not selected by this initiative.\n                  instead: Resolve over an in-memory collection behind a narrow interface.\n                - action: Inventing a precedence rule when several policies match.\n                  reason: Precedence is an unresolved product decision recorded in system_map.unknowns.\n                  instead: Surface ambiguity explicitly and leave the precedence rule to the owner.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - Any provider usage metering client, schema, or record.\n                - src/ratelimit/policy_schema.py\n              rollback: Remove the created resolver and test files.\n              observability: The resolution outcome names the organization and the chosen policy version.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - build\n                - test\n\n  - id: SEAM-ENFORCEMENT\n    name: Window-scoped admission decision\n    description: >-\n      Owns the counting of requests inside a window against the effective policy\n      and the allow or deny verdict for each request.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Decide allow or deny for a request against the effective policy within the\n      window. Does not define policies and does not emit telemetry.\n    consumes:\n      - effective policy for an organization\n      - request arrival\n    produces:\n      - admission decision\n    owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n    independent_proof: >-\n      Given a fixed effective policy of 100 per window, the first 100 requests\n      are allowed and request 101 in the same window is denied, with no telemetry\n      sink attached.\n    decision_ids:\n      - DEC-NO-INFRA-SELECTION\n      - DEC-WINDOW-SEMANTICS\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Derive the request count from provider usage metering counters.\n        reason: >-\n          Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope, and borrowing its\n          counters would place the denial decision on the far side of the boundary.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-ENFORCEMENT\n      name: Enforcement lane\n      owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-DENY-101\n          observable_state: >-\n            After 100 allowed requests in one window, request 101 is denied.\n          proof: Admission test suite drives 101 requests against a 100-per-window policy.\n          requires:\n            - effective policy for an organization\n          produces:\n            - admission decision\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260916-admission-decision\n              title: Deny request 101 after 100 allowed in the same window\n              goal: >-\n                Count requests within a window against the effective policy and\n                deny once the limit is exceeded.\n              done_condition: >-\n                With an effective policy of 100 per window, requests 1 through\n                100 are allowed and request 101 in the same window is denied;\n                the counter is scoped per organization and per window.\n              effort: M\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on:\n                - T-20260916-policy-resolver\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/admission.py\n                - tests/ratelimit/test_admission.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: An effective policy of 100 requests per window for an organization.\n                  when: Requests 1 through 100 arrive in the same window.\n                  then: Every one of those requests is allowed.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: 100 requests already allowed in the current window.\n                  when: Request 101 arrives in the same window.\n                  then: The request is denied and the counter is not incremented past the limit.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: The first 100 requests in a window are allowed.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_admission.py -k allows_first_100 -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Request 101 in the same window is denied.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_admission.py -k denies_101 -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: The whole admission suite passes.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_admission.py -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Reading provider usage metering counters to decide admission.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope; the denial\n                    decision must not depend on it.\n                  instead: Count against this initiative's own window counter behind its interface.\n                - action: Selecting Redis or another counter store.\n                  reason: Production storage is not selected by this initiative.\n                  instead: Keep the counter behind an interface with an in-memory test substrate.\n                - action: Emitting telemetry from inside the decision function.\n                  reason: Telemetry is SEAM-TELEMETRY's responsibility and would blur the seam.\n                  instead: Return a structured decision and let the telemetry seam observe it.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - Any provider usage metering client, schema, or record.\n                - src/ratelimit/policy_schema.py\n                - src/ratelimit/resolver.py\n              rollback: Remove the created admission and test files.\n              observability: The decision carries organization, window, count, and limit.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - build\n                - test\n\n  - id: SEAM-TELEMETRY\n    name: Denial reason and decision telemetry\n    description: >-\n      Owns the stable denial reason contract and the emission of decision\n      telemetry that matches the decision actually made.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Expose a stable denial reason and emit decision telemetry that matches it.\n      This telemetry describes admission decisions and is explicitly not a usage\n      meter and not a replacement for provider-owned metering.\n    consumes:\n      - admission decision\n    produces:\n      - stable denial reason\n      - decision telemetry event\n    owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n    independent_proof: >-\n      A denial yields a reason code that is stable across runs, and the emitted\n      telemetry event matches that same decision field for field.\n    decision_ids:\n      - DEC-METERING-BOUNDARY\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Emit the decision onto the provider usage metering stream.\n        reason: >-\n          That crosses the stated boundary and would make this initiative a\n          partial usage meter, which the blueprint places out of scope.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-TELEMETRY\n      name: Telemetry lane\n      owner: UNASSIGNED pending named owner\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-REASON-TELEMETRY\n          observable_state: >-\n            A denial returns a stable reason and emits one matching decision\n            telemetry event.\n          proof: Telemetry test suite asserts reason stability and event-to-decision agreement.\n          requires:\n            - admission decision\n          produces:\n            - stable denial reason\n            - decision telemetry event\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260916-denial-telemetry\n              title: Stable denial reason with matching decision telemetry\n              goal: >-\n                Give every denial a stable reason code and emit one decision\n                telemetry event that agrees with the decision.\n              done_condition: >-\n                A denial returns the same reason code on repeated runs, exactly\n                one telemetry event is emitted per decision, the event fields\n                agree with the decision, and no event is written to any provider\n                usage metering sink.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on:\n                - T-20260916-admission-decision\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/telemetry.py\n                - tests/ratelimit/test_telemetry.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: A request denied for exceeding the window limit.\n                  when: The denial is returned twice for the same condition.\n                  then: The same stable reason code is returned both times.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: An admission decision is made.\n                  when: Telemetry is emitted for that decision.\n                  then: >-\n                    Exactly one event is emitted to the decision telemetry sink\n                    and its fields match the decision.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: The denial reason code is stable across repeated denials.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_telemetry.py -k stable_reason -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: One emitted event per decision, matching its fields.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_telemetry.py -k matching_event -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: The whole telemetry suite passes.\n                  bash: python3 -m pytest tests/ratelimit/test_telemetry.py -q\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Writing decision events to a provider usage metering sink.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope; decision\n                    telemetry must not be presented or routed as usage data.\n                  instead: Emit to this initiative's own decision telemetry interface.\n                - action: Adding billable-usage fields such as metered units or cost.\n                  reason: Those fields belong to provider-owned metering, not to this seam.\n                  instead: Carry only decision fields: organization, policy version, reason, outcome.\n                - action: Selecting a hosted observability vendor or exporter.\n                  reason: Deployment infrastructure is not selected by this initiative.\n                  instead: Emit behind a sink interface with a recording test double.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - Any provider usage metering client, schema, sink, or record.\n                - src/ratelimit/admission.py\n              rollback: Remove the created telemetry and test files.\n              observability: >-\n                The decision telemetry event is the observability surface; it is\n                scoped to admission decisions only.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - build\n                - test\n                - maintain\n\nsteel_thread:\n  - SEAM-POLICY\n  - SEAM-RESOLUTION\n  - SEAM-ENFORCEMENT\n  - SEAM-TELEMETRY\n\nobjections:\n  - id: OBJ-NO-OWNER\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      No seam, swimlane, or decision owner is named anywhere in the source\n      blueprint. Every owner field carries an explicit unassigned marker rather\n      than an invented identity. Named owners are required before review.\n  - id: OBJ-WINDOW-SEMANTICS\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      Fixed versus sliding window is undecided (DEC-WINDOW-SEMANTICS), and it\n      changes what \"the same window\" means in steel thread step 3, so the\n      enforcement done-condition is not yet fully determined.\n  - id: OBJ-PRECEDENCE\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      The blueprint requires exactly one effective policy but states no\n      precedence rule for several matching policies. The resolver leaf surfaces\n      ambiguity explicitly instead of inventing precedence.\n  - id: OBJ-FIXTURE-EVIDENCE\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      The only evidence source declares itself fixture input and not\n      documentation of shipped behavior, so the system map is proposed rather\n      than verified against a running system.\n"}}}
