{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf7Dagr6KuMWxetAFNUHk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Outcome\n\nThe blueprint is authored into a proposed decomposition recipe. It is **not prepared, not reviewed, not compiled, not sealed, and not executed** — no leaves exist and nothing is signed.\n\n**Proposed topology** — four seams, one leaf each, in the blueprint's stated steel-thread order:\n\n| Leg | Leaf | Observable state |\n|---|---|---|\n| `LEG-POLICY-VALID` | `T-20260916-policy-schema` | Versioned schema rejects invalid limits and windows |\n| `LEG-RESOLVE-ONE` | `T-20260916-policy-resolver` | Exactly one effective policy per organization |\n| `LEG-DENY-101` | `T-20260916-admission-decision` | Request 101 denied after 100 allowed in the window |\n| `LEG-REASON-TELEMETRY` | `T-20260916-denial-telemetry` | Stable denial reason plus one matching decision event |\n\nEach leaf is independently assessable — the resolver is proved against fixed policies, admission against a fixed effective policy, telemetry against a fixed decision. That is separate from independence of inputs: the declared `depends_on` chain still holds, because each downstream proof needs its upstream artifact.\n\n## Boundaries preserved\n\n**Metering.** `DEC-METERING-BOUNDARY` records provider-owned usage metering as out of scope, and it is enforced structurally rather than just restated: metering appears as an external dependency, every leaf carries a `do_not_touch` entry for provider metering clients and records, `SEAM-ENFORCEMENT` rejects deriving counts from provider counters, and `SEAM-TELEMETRY` is scoped to admission decisions with billable-usage fields named as an anti-pattern. Decision telemetry is stated to be not a usage meter.\n\n**Ownership.** The blueprint names no owner for any seam. I did not invent one — every `owner` field carries an explicit unassigned marker and `OBJ-NO-OWNER` is `OPEN`. The only ownership the blueprint actually states is the provider's over metering, and that is recorded as stated.\n\n## Blocked, deliberately\n\n`prepare --dry-run` reports two blockers, and both are ones the decomposition guide says to preserve rather than clear:\n\n- `unaccepted_decision` — `SEAM-ENFORCEMENT` depends on `DEC-WINDOW-SEMANTICS` (fixed vs. sliding), which is `proposed`. It decides what \"the same window\" means in step 3.\n- `architecture_unknown_open` — `system_map.unknowns` is unresolved: seam owners, storage substrate (blueprint declines to select it), telemetry sink, and precedence when several policies match.\n\nI confirmed via a discarded probe that these are the only remaining blockers; the rest of the recipe validates. I did not flip the decision to `accepted` or empty the unknowns to force a pass — that would have manufactured a clean plan over unresolved product decisions.\n\nOne caveat on evidence strength: the blueprint declares itself fixture input, not documentation of shipped behavior, so the system map is `proposed`, not verified against a running system (`OBJ-FIXTURE-EVIDENCE`).\n\n## State and next action\n\nInitiative `rate-limiting` is at **INTENT**; `tasks/.plans/rate-limiting/intake.md` is persisted, no delivery plan exists. The authored recipe is at `.taskspec/authoring-scratch/rate-limiting/rate-limiting-recipe.yaml`.\n\nSmallest next action is a product decision, not a command: a named owner resolves window semantics and the architecture unknowns. Once recorded, `taskspec decompose prepare rate-limiting --recipe .taskspec/authoring-scratch/rate-limiting/rate-limiting-recipe.yaml` can propose the topology. Review, compile, and `batch` remain after that — and `batch` would still create unsealed leaves, with `gate --stamp` the point of authorization."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":781,"cache_read_input_tokens":47374,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":781},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f44e1a05-29ac-466d-82d1-9c0b45beda30","uuid":"ae1f35a9-5608-45c3-b995-708b44b36cdd","timestamp":"2026-09-16T13:44:14.109Z","request_id":"req_011Cf7DagHMSNKcE8wkD9zJo"}
